From 18a99c631ce2f2d7aff35a91f93ae0c89804467e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: MiaAI-Lab <MiaAI-Lab@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 08:21:10 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 184/185] glm: DFlash2 at full GLM-5.3's shape
 (incoai/GLM-5.3-DFlash2) on glm_moe_dsa

The drafter's shape is read from its config.json: GLM-5.3-Flash's (D 4096, 5 layers, 32 query heads, the 4-stream
mean taps after 5/14/24/33/42, theta 1e4; the old constants) or full GLM-5.3's (D 6144, 6 layers, 64 query heads of
128 over 8 KV heads, q wider than D, conv kernel projections 1536 rows, fc 6 x 6144 wide, theta 1e6, taps after layers
5/19/33/47/61/75 of glm_moe_dsa's one residual stream). glm_dflash.cu's width-dependent kernels (block_qkv, conv,
attn_part, attn_merge, sumn) are templates: df_* at the Flash shape (bit-identical to before on a GPU check), dg_* at
the full one. Taps take a layer list (DSpark's by default); the prompt path taps and ingests DSA chunks for any drafter
that taps the one stream (dsaTaps). A drafter whose shape does not match the target is refused.

Credits: the drafter is Inco AI's DFlash2 for GLM-5.3 (https://huggingface.co/incoai/GLM-5.3-DFlash2, revision
8f02251dc71a9da2053dfc15bfa293fbee5579b0, Apache-2.0), read unmodified from its BF16 safetensors and quantized in device
memory at load; no converted copy is written. The DFlash architecture is Z Lab's (https://github.com/z-lab/dflash, MIT).
The engine side extends the Zig DFlash2 drafter authored by Ash Hart (@ashhart) and the TensorFold contributors.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01UQVvNktFCvQrvpNUbqtqBX
